<title>UNITED NATIONS: China kills U.N. peacekeeping force for Guatemala.</title>
<headline>China kills U.N. peacekeeping force for Guatemala.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>China cast its first U.N. Security Council veto in nearly 25 years on Friday, killing a resolution authorizing a small U.N. peacekeeping mission for Guatemala because of that country's ties with Taiwan.</p>
<p>The other 14 Security Council members voted in favor of sending 155 military observers to verify the Central American country's new U.N.-brokered peace accord. But a negative vote by China -- one of five permanent council members with veto power -- killed the measure.</p>
</text>
